„­bible_version£KJV¤book%§chapter	¨sections•…¤book%§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ²The burden of the word of the LORD in the land of Hadrach, and Damascus shall be the rest thereof: when the eyes of man, as of all the tribes of Israel, shall be toward the LORD.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOAnd Hamath also shall border thereby; Tyrus, and Zidon, though it be very wise.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd Tyrus did build herself a strong hold, and heaped up silver as the dust, and fine gold as the mire of the streets.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpBehold, the Lord will cast her out, and he will smite her power in the sea; and she shall be devoured with fire.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book%§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÊAshkelon shall see it, and fear; Gaza also shall see it, and be very sorrowful, and Ekron; for her expectation shall be ashamed; and the king shall perish from Gaza, and Ashkelon shall not be inhabited.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd a bastard shall dwell in Ashdod, and I will cut off the pride of the Philistines.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÔAnd I will take away his blood out of his mouth, and his abominations from between his teeth: but he that remaineth, even he, shall be for our God, and he shall be as a governor in Judah, and Ekron as a Jebusite.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑAnd I will encamp about mine house because of the army, because of him that passeth by, and because of him that returneth: and no oppressor shall pass through them any more: for now have I seen with mine eyes.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book%§chapter	«first_verse	ªlast_verse
