…¤book%§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrAs for thee also, by the blood of thy covenant I have sent forth thy prisoners out of the pit wherein is no water.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpTurn you to the strong hold, ye prisoners of hope: even to day do I declare that I will render double unto thee;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£when I have bent Judah for me, filled the bow with Ephraim, and raised up thy sons, O Zion, against thy sons, O Greece, and made thee as the sword of a mighty man.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book%§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¨And the LORD shall be seen over them, and his arrow shall go forth as the lightning: and the Lord GOD shall blow the trumpet, and shall go with whirlwinds of the south.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ×The LORD of hosts shall defend them; and they shall devour, and subdue with sling stones; and they shall drink, and make a noise as through wine; and they shall be filled like bowls, and as the corners of the altar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And the LORD their God shall save them in that day as the flock of his people: for they shall be as the stones of a crown, lifted up as an ensign upon his land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{For how great is his goodness, and how great is his beauty! corn shall make the young men cheerful, and new wine the maids.¦layout ªlast_verse